{
 "How Med-Arb works at Adjudix": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Agreement — the parties opt into the hybrid procedure in their contract or after the dispute arises.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Mediation phase — a mediator from the Adjudix panel works with the parties, jointly and in private sessions, to find terms both can accept.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Settlement — if the parties settle, the terms are recorded as a consent award, with the same status and effect as an arbitral award.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Conversion — if mediation does not succeed within the agreed period, the matter moves to the arbitration phase under the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Award — the tribunal decides the outstanding issues and makes a final, enforceable award.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "The confidentiality question": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "The hard part of any hybrid process is what happens to information shared in mediation. A party that speaks candidly to a mediator in private session should know in advance whether that same person may later decide the case. The Adjudix Code answers this by offering Med-Arb in two kinds, chosen in the clause or at the start of the case.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Same-Neutral Med-Arb (Option A) — the mediator continues as arbitrator if mediation fails, already knowing the negotiations that took place. It is quicker and cheaper, because no one has to learn the case afresh, and the parties waive any objection based on what the neutral learnt in mediation.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Separate-Neutral Med-Arb (Option B) — a different neutral conducts the arbitration, and nothing said in mediation goes to the arbitrator. It suits parties who want to speak with complete freedom in mediation.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "A silent clause — where the agreement does not say which kind applies, the Code deems it Same-Neutral Med-Arb. Parties who want separate neutrals should say so in their clause.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Why the law supports it": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Section {0} of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, {1} expressly allows an arbitral tribunal to use mediation, conciliation, or other procedures to encourage settlement, and to record a settlement as an award on agreed terms. A hybrid procedure therefore sits squarely within the existing law; it does not depend on any novel interpretation.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "When Med-Arb works best": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Long-term commercial relationships — supply, distribution, joint ventures — where preserving goodwill matters.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Construction and infrastructure contracts with many small, technical disputes.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Family-owned businesses and shareholder disagreements, where a settlement saves the business.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Any dispute where one party fears that mediation is only a delaying tactic.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Choosing the neutrals": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "The success of a hybrid process depends heavily on who conducts each phase. A good mediator is patient, curious, and skilled at helping parties see their real interests; a good arbitrator is rigorous, decisive, and careful about procedure. Some professionals do both well, but the roles are different. At Adjudix, the parties may choose the mediator and the arbitrator separately from the Professional Panel, or ask the Secretariat to propose names suited to the subject matter — an engineer for a construction dispute, a chartered accountant for an accounts dispute.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "The time allowed for the mediation phase is agreed at the outset, typically between two and six weeks. A fixed window keeps everyone focused: the parties know that if they do not settle, a binding decision will follow, which is often the strongest incentive to settle of all.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "What it costs": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Because many hybrid matters settle in the mediation phase, the overall cost is frequently lower than a full arbitration. Where the case does convert, the work done in mediation — narrowing the issues, agreeing facts, exchanging documents — usually shortens the arbitration that follows. Fees for each phase are set out in the Adjudix fee schedule, so parties can plan for both outcomes.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "The result": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "Parties get the cost and relationship benefits of a negotiated outcome without the risk of an inconclusive process. That combination — resolution first, then assured implementation — is why the hybrid model is the lead service at Adjudix.": "/knowledge/blog/hybrid-adr-med-arb",
 "From Award to Recovery: How Arbitral Awards Are Implemented in India and Abroad | Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Implementation · {0} min read": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Winning an award is a milestone, not the finish line. A party that has spent months in arbitration needs the award to turn into money, property, or performance. Many institutions stop at the award. Adjudix treats implementation as part of the service — because for the party who has won, it is the part that matters most.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Voluntary compliance comes first": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Most awards are honoured without a court ever being involved, particularly where the losing party is a business that values its reputation and relationships. A structured demand, a clear computation of the amount due with interest, and a realistic payment plan often achieve more than immediate litigation.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Enforcing a domestic award": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Under Section {0} of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, {1}, once the three-month period for challenge has expired — or a challenge has been dismissed — the award is enforced in the same manner as a decree of a civil court. Filing a challenge does not automatically stay the award; the court must grant a stay, usually on terms such as depositing the amount awarded.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Enforcement follows the execution procedure of the Code of Civil Procedure: attachment and sale of property, attachment of bank accounts and debts owed to the award-debtor, and other measures the court may order. The Supreme Court has confirmed that an award can be executed directly wherever the assets are located, without first obtaining a transfer from the court that has jurisdiction over the arbitration.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Enforcing a foreign award in India": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Awards made in a country that India recognises under the New York Convention are enforced under Part II of the Act. The court can refuse enforcement only on narrow grounds — such as incapacity, an invalid agreement, lack of proper notice, or conflict with the fundamental policy of Indian law. Once the court is satisfied, the foreign award is deemed a decree and is executed accordingly.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Enforcing an Indian award abroad": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Because more than {0} countries are party to the New York Convention, an award made in India can usually be enforced where the award-debtor's assets actually are. The process follows the local law of that country, typically requiring the original or a certified copy of the award and the arbitration agreement, with certified translations where needed. Local counsel, asset tracing, and coordinated filings across jurisdictions are often the difference between a paper victory and a real one.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "What Adjudix implementation covers": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Review of the award and the computation of the amount due, including interest and costs.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Structured demand and negotiated compliance where possible.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Identification of assets and the right forum for execution.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Coordination of execution proceedings in India, and of recognition and enforcement abroad through partner counsel.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Implementation of mediated and conciliated settlements, not only arbitral awards.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "Dispute resolved, and implemented": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "That is the promise behind the Adjudix tagline: Dispute Resolved & Implemented under one Roof. Resolution and implementation are designed together, from the first consultation to the final recovery.": "/knowledge/blog/implementing-arbitral-awards",
 "The Mediation Act, {0}: What It Changes and What It Means for You | Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Until {0}, mediation in India rested on a patchwork: court-annexed mediation under the Code of Civil Procedure, conciliation under Part III of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, {1}, and pre-institution mediation under the Commercial Courts Act, {2}. The Mediation Act, {3} brings mediation under one law for the first time, and gives a settlement reached in mediation real legal force.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Pre-litigation mediation": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Before filing a civil or commercial suit, the parties may, voluntarily and by mutual consent, try to settle the dispute through pre-litigation mediation — whether or not their contract contains a mediation clause. The aim is to resolve disputes before they reach an already crowded court system.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Time limits": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "A mediation under the Act must be completed within {0} days from the date the parties first appear before the mediator. The parties may extend this by consent for a further period of up to {1} days. The fixed window keeps mediation from becoming a delaying tactic.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Everything said, shown, or offered in mediation is confidential. The mediator, the parties, and everyone else involved may not disclose it, and it cannot be relied on as evidence in later arbitral or court proceedings. This is what lets parties speak candidly in private sessions.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "The mediated settlement agreement": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "If the parties settle, they sign a mediated settlement agreement, which the mediator authenticates. Under the Act it is final and binding on the parties, and it can be enforced in the same manner as a judgment or decree of a court.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "A challenge is allowed only on narrow grounds — fraud, corruption, impersonation, or that the dispute was not fit for mediation — and must be brought within a limited period after the settlement is received.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Online and community mediation": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "The Act recognises online mediation, conducted through electronic means with the parties' consent, on the same footing as mediation in person. It also provides for community mediation, to settle disputes likely to affect peace and harmony among residents of a locality.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "What cannot be mediated": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "A schedule to the Act lists disputes not fit for mediation — among them criminal prosecutions, matters affecting the rights of third parties who are not part of the mediation, and certain disputes reserved for statutory bodies. When in doubt, the free consultation at Adjudix will tell you whether your dispute qualifies.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "The Mediation Council of India": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "The Act establishes the Mediation Council of India to register mediators, recognise mediation service providers and mediation institutes, and set standards for training and conduct. Its provisions are being brought into force in stages, so always check which parts apply on the date of your mediation.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Mediation at Adjudix": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Adjudix mediation follows the Mediation Act, {0} and the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure. And where the parties want a guaranteed outcome, Hybrid Med-Arb adds an arbitration phase if mediation does not settle the dispute.": "/knowledge/blog/mediation-act-2023",
 "Online, Offline, or Both: Choosing How Your Hearing Runs | Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Online & Offline · {0} min read": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Few changes have reshaped dispute resolution as quickly as the move to online proceedings. What began as a necessity is now a choice — and a good one in many cases. But it is a choice: some disputes are best heard in a room, and many benefit from a mix of both.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "The legal footing": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Indian law recognises electronic records, electronic signatures, and contracts formed by electronic means under the Information Technology Act, {0}. The Arbitration and Conciliation Act lets the parties — or, failing agreement, the tribunal — decide the procedure, including where and how hearings are held, and the Mediation Act, {1} expressly recognises online mediation. An award made after online hearings is as valid as one made after hearings in person.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "When online works best": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Document-heavy disputes where oral evidence is limited.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Parties, counsel, or witnesses in different cities or countries.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Procedural hearings and case management conferences.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Mediation sessions, especially private sessions with each party.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Small and medium claims, where travel would be a large share of the cost.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "When to meet in person": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Cases that turn on the credibility of key witnesses under cross-examination.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Complex technical evidence that benefits from site visits or physical exhibits.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Settlement meetings where the parties' presence in one room changes the dynamic.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Hybrid hearings": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Many cases combine the two: procedural hearings and most witnesses online, the key witnesses in person, or a tribunal sitting physically with some participants joining remotely. The tribunal sets the format at the first case management conference, after hearing the parties.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Making online hearings fair": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "An online hearing must give every party a full opportunity to present its case, just as a physical one does. Good practice includes a test session before the hearing, a protocol on who may be present in each participant's room, rules for sharing documents on screen, and an agreed method for witness examination — including how a witness's documents are controlled while they give evidence. Hearings are recorded or transcribed where the tribunal so directs.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Data security matters too. Case documents should be exchanged through a secure platform, not personal email, and access should be limited to the parties, their counsel, and the tribunal. These safeguards are built into the Adjudix ODR Platform and set out in the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Cost and time": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Online hearings remove travel, accommodation, and venue costs and make it far easier to find dates that suit everyone — which often brings the final hearing forward by weeks. For small and medium claims, these savings can be a significant share of the total cost of the dispute.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "How Adjudix runs it": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "The Adjudix ODR Platform handles filing, service of documents, scheduling, and virtual hearings, with secure storage of the case record. Offline proceedings use the same procedure and the same Code. Whichever format the parties choose, the rules, the timelines, and the standards are identical — only the room changes.": "/knowledge/blog/online-and-offline-hearings",
 "Why Institutional ADR: The Adjudix Model | Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "About Adjudix · {0} min read": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Parties can resolve disputes ad hoc — appointing arbitrators themselves and managing the process on their own. Ad hoc arbitration works when everything goes smoothly. When it does not, there is no one to appoint a replacement arbitrator, fix a timetable, hold fees, or keep the process on track, and the parties end up in court arguing about procedure. An institution exists to prevent that.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Resolution and implementation, under one roof": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Most institutions end their role with the award. Adjudix does not. Our model treats the dispute as resolved only when the outcome has been implemented — the award paid, the settlement performed, the order complied with — in India or anywhere in the world. That is what “Dispute Resolved & Implemented under one Roof” means.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Every mechanism, matched to the dispute": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Adjudix administers arbitration, mediation, conciliation, Lok Adalat-style settlement sittings, emergency arbitration, corporate ADR, and — as our flagship — the hybrid Med-Arb model, which attempts settlement first and assures a binding outcome either way. Proceedings run online, offline, or both.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "A professional panel, organised by profession": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Our Professional Panel brings together lawyers, chartered accountants and company secretaries, and engineers of every discipline, so that each dispute is heard by someone who understands its subject matter. Every panelist discloses conflicts before appointment and is bound by the Moral Principles that form the Preamble to the Adjudix Code. We deliberately do not publish photographs of our arbitrators, to protect the independence of every proceeding.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Published rules, published fees": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Every case is governed by the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0}, and charged under a published fee schedule, so parties know the procedure and the cost before they begin. No party should be negotiating process after a dispute has already started.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Ad hoc or institutional: the practical difference": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "In an ad hoc arbitration, the parties must agree on every procedural step themselves, and when they disagree, a court must often step in — to appoint an arbitrator, to replace one who withdraws, or to resolve a dispute about fees. Each trip to court adds months. An institution resolves these questions administratively, under rules the parties agreed to in advance: the Secretariat appoints or replaces arbitrators, holds and accounts for fees, monitors timelines, and scrutinises awards for form before they are issued.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Institutional arbitration also gives the parties a clear record of the procedure followed, which matters if the award is later challenged or needs to be enforced abroad.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Built to be trusted": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Trust in an institution comes from what it does consistently: disclosing conflicts, keeping proceedings confidential, applying the same Code to every party regardless of size, and accounting transparently for fees. Adjudix is built on these commitments, set out in the Moral Principles that open the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, and backed by a grievance mechanism for anyone who believes they have not been met.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Before and after the dispute": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
 "Adjudix also works before disputes arise, through contract and arbitration clause drafting, and builds the profession through six certification tracks, apprenticeships and internships, and five kinds of membership. Together, these make Adjudix a complete dispute resolution institution — from the clause, to the resolution, to the recovery.": "/knowledge/blog/the-adjudix-model",
